A||||5||Cozmo||Water pump brand suggestions?||||1||
Z||000000||Cozmo||02-27-2001||08:02 AM||||Hi list,<BR>I'm fixing a stripped water pump bolt on my '85 2M6 and while I've got it all apart I figure it's a good idea to put a new pump on. I've found 3 manufacturers so far, they are:<BR>Airtex $35 (new)<BR>A1 Cardone (reman.) $15 + $4 core<BR>TRW (new-says "OE") $40<BR>Which one is the best? I'll stay away from reman. units, I am leaning towards the TRW.<BR>Don't know if it has a metal impeller yet (will look at it today).<BR>Also, are NAPA belts the best?<BR>This hasn't been too bad of a job so far, just had to keep track of all those weird bolt sizes and rip out that %&*@# itchy fiberglass insulation...<BR>Thanks,<BR>Cozmo<p>[This message has been edited by Cozmo (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||02-27-2001||05:24 PM||||Didn't get any advice, so I got the Airtex pump and a Gates belt. Now to re-assemble. <BR>I've read as much as I can find in the archives on this job.  Some of the bolts go into the water jacket, what is the best way to seal them? Any other tricks I should know?<BR>Cozmo||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||02-27-2001||08:22 PM||||To seal the bolts, clean up the threads on the bolts (run a tap in the holes if you have one) and put high temp RTV (orange stuff) on the bolt thread.  Do it sparingly as too much creates a terrible mess.  Did the Airtex have a plastic, cast or steel impeller?  I got my pump from the FieroStore and it had a plastic impeller but seemed to work okay.  Then again, I only put 450 mi on it before I junked the motor for other reasons.  I am no expert on Fiero water pumps so I didn't offer my 2cents.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||02-27-2001||09:18 PM||||I have seen cases in which a plastic impeller "loses its grip" on the pump shaft.  The shaft rotates but the impeller doesn't.  Externally the pump looks OK, but it doesn't pump.  Someone (88DatabaseGuy?) showed us an example of this problem at a club meeting.<P>Sorry I didn't read your message sooner.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cozmo||02-27-2001||10:33 PM||||I cleaned up the bolts and holes with a tap and die set, got all the mounting surfaces prepped and cleaned. I'll use hi temp RTV (sparingly!) when I put it together tomorrow. <BR>The Airtex has a steel impeller.<BR>After working on this, I'm amazed what a klugey design this is. 12 bolts of 3 different sizes and 3 different torque settings!<BR>Oh well... <BR>Thanks,<BR>Cozmo ||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTZ34||02-28-2001||01:10 AM||||Cozmo, thanks for the tip on the water pump.  Like PBody, I don't care for the plastic impeller.  While it certainly is lighter it is not stronger.  I don't need the light wieghted one as I'm not trying to rev to 10K.  thanks again.  BTW, its probably obvious but I used the sealer on the metal surfaces for the gasket as well (sparingly of course).||||reg||1
